6. bxa5 { White takes the pawn. Do I really need to say what would you play in this position? } 6... Rxa5 { Correct! If you find it, you definetely knows how the rook♖moves. } 7. a4 { Now play Ne8, trying to reroute the knight to the queenside. } { [%csl Ge8][%cal Gf6e8] } 7... Ne8 8. Ba3 { Now play b6, preparing c5, also at the same time, clear out the c7 square for the knight. } { [%csl Gb6][%cal Gb7b6] } 8... b6 9. Bb4 { Bring back the rook here, but if you don't mind, please try EVERY possible move. } 9... Ra8 { We bring the rook back home. } (9... Ra6 { Also good, but please find a better one. }) (9... Ra7 { Also good, but please find a better one. }) (9... Rxa4?? { You sure that is free? }) (9... Rb5?? { Are you the famous Santa Claus? Cause you just gives away the rook. }) (9... Rc5?? { Are you the famous Santa Claus? Cause you just gives away the rook. }) (9... Rxd5?? { You sure that is free? }) 10. a5 { Now play c5, attacking the bishop. } { [%csl Gc5][%cal Gc7c5] } 10... c5 11. dxc6 { Take back the pawn, please. } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Ge7c6] } 11... Nxc6 { You have completed the whole course for the Orthodox Variation. Good job!🪔 } *

