Take a look at the analysis board for more. } 5... Nc5 { Controlling b3, where the queen likes to go. } { [%csl Bb3][%cal Bc5b3,Bd1b3] } (5... Bd7 { Second most popular move here by Black. } 6. b4?! { Preparing to take on a5, so we take the pawn first. } 6... axb4! { A great response, even tho they say "To take is a MISTAKE". } 7. axb4 { After all, White have a lost of a pawn. } 7... Nxb4! { You might notice the rook is hanging, but it's NOT. The queen is protecting the rook. You might say that after } 8. Rxa8?! { , the queen has to take back and the queen will be just staring at NOTHING. But it's not like that. After } 8... Qxa8 { , look, the queen is at the very open a-file! A very nice chance to own the a-file! }) 6. Qc2 { Developing the queen to a active square. Play a4! } { [%csl Ba4][%cal Ba5a4] } 6... a4 { Gaining more space on the queenside. } 7. Be3 { White tend to trade of the knight, who is guarding b3. But now, we PLACE it on b3! } { [%csl Bb3][%cal Bc5b3] } 7... Nb3 { White's piece's can't move freely now because of our knight. } *

