[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

8. Bd3? { Worse than Nfd2. Now, please play the brilliant-est move here, can you find it? } 8... Na6!! { Great if you found this! The point here, is ... Nb4! attacking the queen who is guarding the knight. } 9. a3? { A huge mistake. This stops Nb4, but it didn't stop...
c4!!! } { [%csl Bb4][%cal Ba3b4,Ba6b4] } 9... c4!! { Sacrificing the pawn!!! } 10. Qxc4 { Now the game is totally winning for us. But we're not done. Play...
Rc8!! } 10... Rc8!! { Attacking the queen! } 11. Qa4 { Now it's time for...
Nc5!!!
You heard it right, sacrificing the knight!!! } { [%csl Bc5][%cal Ba6c5] } 11... Nc5!! 12. Qd1 { Queen takes e8, sacrificing the queen for rook is the best choice for Stockfish.
Now play, Nxd3! } { [%csl Bd3][%cal Bc5d3] } 12... Nxd3+! { Trading off the defender of the knight on e4. } 13. Qxd3 { Now take the knight! } { [%csl Be4][%cal Bf5e4] } 13... Bxe4 { We now have a great position with active pieces. It's -7.3 now! } *

