6. O-O?! { Castling looks normal, but it's actually a mistake. Play c4! } { [%csl Bc4][%cal Bc5c4] } 6... c4 { Taking more space in the queenside. } 7. Bc2 { Now we continue our attack with b4! } { [%csl Bb4][%cal Bb5b4] } 7... b4 { We're taking more and more space! } 8. Ne2 { Now we play Re8! } { [%csl Be8][%cal Bf8e8] } 8... Re8 9. Ng3 { Rerouting the knight to the kingside. Now we take advantage that the f2 pawn is missing with Qb6+! } { [%csl Bb6][%cal Bd8b6] } 9... Qb6+ 10. Kh1 { Now, we play Ng4, planting it deep into enemy's territory! } { [%csl Bg4][%cal Bf6g4] } 10... Ng4 { They can't kick the knight. I'll explain that in a moment. } 11. Qe2 { If h3, we play Nf2+ - a royal fork of the king/queen, forcing them to give up the rook with Rxf2, then we play Qxf2 and we won an exchange.
Now we play c3, attacking the queenside! } { [%csl Bc3][%cal Bc4c3] } 11... c3 { Now we have an aggresive attack on the queenside. Good job!😊 } *

