1. Be2 { Developing the bishop, but it's too too passive. Play O-O to safen your king! } { [%csl Bg8][%cal Be8g8] } 1... O-O 2. Bg5 { Now we strike in the center with c5! } { [%csl Bc5][%cal Bc7c5] } 2... c5 3. d5 { Taking space in the center. Now we play e6, tending to trade off the e-pawn and open up the f-file for the rook. } { [%csl Be6][%cal Be7e6] } 3... e6 4. Qd2 { Declining the trade of pawns. No problem, now we trade them! } { [%csl Bd5][%cal Be6d5] } 4... exd5 5. exd5 { Now we play Qb6! } { [%csl Bb6][%cal Bd8b6] } 5... Qb6 6. Nf3 { Now we continue our development with Bf5! } { [%csl Bf5][%cal Bc8f5] } 6... Bf5 { This position is totally equal. It's hard to see a equal position in the KID!🪔 } *

