[Orientation "black"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

1. h3! { The best move according to Lord Stockfish. Simply castle here. } 1... O-O { We safen our king. } 2. Nf3 { Strike in the center with e5! } { [%csl Be5][%cal Be7e5] } 2... e5 3. d5 { Now we play the absurd Nh5! } { [%csl Bh5][%cal Bf6h5] } 3... Nh5! { We hope to place it on f4. } { [%csl Bf4][%cal Bh5f4] } 4. g3! { They don't allow the knight to be in f4. But here comes f5! } { [%csl Bf5][%cal Bf7f5] } 4... f5 { Opening up the position! } 5. exf5 { Now play gxf5! } { [%csl Bf5][%cal Bg6f5] } 5... gxf5 { Mind that Bxf5 would be a mistake, because of g4! forking the bishop and the knight. } 6. Nh4 { Attacking the f5 pawn. Now we sacrifice...
The KNIGHT!!! With NF4!!! } { [%csl Bf4][%cal Bh5f4] } 6... Nf4!! { Simply brilliant! If gxf4, Qxh5! cause the knight on h5 is no longer protected. } 7. Bd2 { The end of the Makogonov Variation. Good luck winning the game!🪔 } *

